  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate March 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant will fund the upcoming Climate March in the Netherlands, organized by the Climate Crisis Coalition that Greenpeace Netherlands is part of (like Oxfam Novib and 8 other organisations, such as Milieudefensie, FossielVrij NL and DeGoedeZaak).
The hope is to organize a march that will bring together at least 100.000 people. With this march, just before the national elections,  a strongmessage to politicians will be given who will form the new cabinet. Besides, the aim is to influence the voting behavior of voters,to vote for more green and progressive parties. Specifically, the hope is to mobilize a lot of youth, as they will form the first &#x2018;block&#x2019;  of the march.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Greenpeace Nederland</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Greenpeace is an independent, international environmental organisation working for a green, peaceful planet.

As a global organisation, Greanpeace  focuses on solving the most important environmental problems of our time, the loss of biodiversity and the climate crisis. As explained by the counterpart: To tackle these problems, we need to stop using fossil fuels, protect our forests and oceans and make our agriculture sustainable. Greenpeace is committed worldwide to getting exactly those things done. They research, put items on the agenda, talk to companies and politicians and campaign for real solutions. Together with scientists, environmental organisations and local communities.

Greenpeace Netherlands employs about 100 people and has about 2,000 volunteers. Their managing director is Andy Palmen. They have an independent, unpaid Supervisory Board of expert and experienced people.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
